# C006 theory smoke v1 (not an independent gate or performance job)

Before execution freeze examples_v1.json, this protocol, smoke_v1.py and
PROOFS_v1.md through shared evidence/capture.py. Enumerate every unordered
partition on each declared 2/3-symbol alphabet with an independently written
restricted-growth generator. Compute exact projection-feasible partition sets,
swap/rescue edges and bipartition collision covers. Write/flush raw results BEFORE
assertions. Check original and manually reduced graph-gap examples; removal of
either reduced positive destroys obstruction. Do not claim automatic shrinking
or universal minimum across different inference systems.

Also check no-negatives and no-positives variants on every fixture, coarsening
closure on all its feasible partitions and absence of holes in feasible k.
Infinite-factor extension is a proof, not experimentally verified infinity.
No solver/runtime from another branch is imported; only stdlib is used. No
performance claims or timing jobs. On failure retain version and revise with
a new filename. All raw evidence is the shared capture stdout/stderr.
